{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "papers": [
    {
      "id": "8c8e315d-55c9-4262-8a6d-b884ad2e06cb",
      "title": "From Components to Instances: Iterative Composition",
      "templateRef": {
        "id": "exploration",
        "version": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "ada40061-3d12-4cf3-ba56-bda67cd92f32",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Abstract",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3514ab07-d379-4747-9988-3230b308437d",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Working proposal only. This paper investigates whether repeated, constraint-guided composition can grow existing components into an intent-specific instance. No experimental findings are claimed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "fb5524bb-e76b-4e24-b284-059164724ddf",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Introduction and Research Question",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8c1ff699-b773-4080-a1b6-1e8610b8f5d1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Can an iterative algorithm use the available components’ capabilities, interfaces, dependencies, and constraints to propose composites, represent viable assemblies at higher planes, and continue until a specified instance intent is satisfied? The user describes this as System 1 thinking guided by the components’ genetic makeup. These are working metaphors whose technical meanings remain to be defined.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "5f6847e6-7b31-450b-a94e-c84cb8fb4a70",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Background and Related Work",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "bc883e21-5f25-4985-9a38-10a632c85095",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Not researched yet.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "36564a72-bc15-4caa-8245-08569feb38ed",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Provisional Hypotheses and Predictions",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "585b9190-0491-45f0-8082-2c168bf3666b",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Proposed hypothesis: capability-guided candidate selection, explicit compatibility checks, and feedback from validation can produce increasingly useful assemblies while reusing previously validated pieces. This hypothesis is untested.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "e97f1124-88ab-4539-b89f-a7a668698d5b",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Assumptions and Alternative Explanations",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "dec86d48-4ed0-4e64-98c3-3b0aa2573650",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open assumptions: component descriptions contain enough information to judge useful combinations; local compatibility can be supplemented by assembly-level behavior checks; repeated composition improves requirement coverage rather than merely adding layers. Compare against predefined recipes and unguided composition.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "666b018b-8f23-4275-842b-91461c36f62b",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Methods of Inquiry",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c1ddd301-fe97-4e92-9605-011d6cf16bc6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Proposed loop for discussion: identify an unresolved requirement; inspect available pieces; propose a candidate assembly; validate its interfaces and behavior; reject or revise failures; expose a successful assembly as a reusable higher-layer item; reassess the remaining requirements. Define evaluation tasks, baselines, budgets, and stopping rules before testing.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "09d7eae8-9754-4ff1-bd27-ab5c570abadf",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Results and Evidence",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3efd32f1-98f1-4182-a392-03d5c7d5ae77",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No experiment has been run for this research question. Existing canvas demonstrations do not establish that this general algorithm works.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "6060a616-7552-40d6-b5da-83f74b54577b",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Discussion and Critical Evaluation",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c25e1c47-7d0e-42bc-b7d0-7e3e765710d5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "To be developed after defining the mechanism and collecting evidence.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9d503356-0f70-49b8-975a-f903e02a88a6",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Limitations and Validity",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "88953fb3-c4b2-4bd3-bb95-2807bdd996b3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compatibility alone does not establish usefulness or correctness. More abstraction layers do not necessarily indicate progress. Hidden dependencies, inaccurate capability descriptions, and failed assumptions may prevent a viable assembly.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "35f04804-2381-47ec-bbf0-232aba702748",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conclusion",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9d5a4e84-fcff-42a6-aae9-bf0026341f32",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Unresolved. This is a research direction, not an established capability.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "ded991d5-d364-4b87-942d-073871d3b06e",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open Questions and Next Tests",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "63d926be-4d83-4191-8826-2932c2cc6e82",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What precisely does System 1 mean here: rapid retrieval of known assemblies, learned candidate ranking, or another mechanism? What constitutes the genetic makeup of a component? What measurable requirement coverage, validation evidence, and resource limits define a substantial instance and stop the iteration?",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1a5d0a77-2f00-411a-b08d-cc69704a9cc4",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reproducibility and Disclosures",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c7c32648-61ac-4758-abb5-0202f059d928",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Initial idea supplied by the user; organization and provisional wording assisted by AI. No external literature review or experimental evaluation has yet been performed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "21db178f-a124-4bad-b22a-913621b84bf2",
          "type": "heading",
